  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Nebius is riding strong enterprise demand for low-cost open-source AI, with cloud capacity routinely sold out before construction, challenging legacy hyperscalers on price. A recent selloff on fears that Meta may offload excess compute highlighted competitive nerves, yet retail sentiment remains bullish on the neocloud opportunity. High GPU rental rates provide a near-term tailwind, but the capital-hungry buildout makes the stock a battleground where growth optimism clashes with worries about funding costs in a higher-rate world.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is executing aggressively—pursuing a UK data-center expansion, launching a Physical AI Living Lab for robotics startups with Nvidia tools, and upgrading the cloud platform. Nasdaq-100 inclusion signals a deliberate push to capture passive institutional flows. Pre-selling capacity before it goes live lends operational credibility, but the massive capex plan raises scrutiny of capital-allocation discipline. Market confidence hinges on whether the team can sustain rapid scaling without overextending the balance sheet amid elevated financing costs.",
